WEBVTT

00:01.030 --> 00:05.980
Let me out. Someone let me out.

00:13.880 --> 00:15.130
Who are you?

00:15.490 --> 00:17.880
Are you a traveler who 
was deceived by Emily?

00:18.680 --> 00:20.620
If you know that, then...

00:21.170 --> 00:22.920
I'm not a traveler.

00:23.600 --> 00:24.870
I came here...

00:26.170 --> 00:28.090
to free her from this place.

00:39.220 --> 00:41.140
This is Emily?

00:42.560 --> 00:45.030
The researchers who joined forces with FUG

00:45.030 --> 00:48.430
began two research projects 
related to Ignition Weapons.

00:49.850 --> 00:55.980
One was to turn a living human into 
an Ignition Weapon, and the other...

00:57.230 --> 01:02.110
was to dissolve a person who 
had become an Ignition Weapon.

01:03.230 --> 01:04.670
Both projects were a success.

01:06.870 --> 01:10.380
The researchers planned to dispose of 
everything once the experiments concluded,

01:10.380 --> 01:12.860
but a female researcher opposed the idea,

01:12.860 --> 01:15.800
and Emily was allowed 
to live inside a flask.

01:17.710 --> 01:21.900
The two Workshop Battle hosts 
approached the female researcher,

01:21.900 --> 01:23.930
used their position

01:24.260 --> 01:29.380
to trap Emily inside a giant tank, 
and built equipment to control her.

01:30.980 --> 01:36.450
Their goal was to use Emily to gather the 
people they needed for their research.

01:36.880 --> 01:41.150
But their ultimate goal was total control 
over the residents of the Tower.

01:42.600 --> 01:47.020
In order to gather funds to distribute 
devices and conduct their research,

01:47.020 --> 01:48.210
they allied with a merchant group

01:48.760 --> 01:51.230
and allowed them to interfere 
with the Workshop Battle.

01:53.390 --> 01:58.040
After the Workshop Battle ends,
in order to secretly transport Emily,

01:58.040 --> 02:01.880
they were to receive this hyper-compression 
flask from the merchants...

02:02.720 --> 02:05.970
Um, this isn't Emily.

02:05.970 --> 02:10.140
She said she's alive and trapped inside a tank.

02:10.140 --> 02:11.480
She asked for help!

02:11.890 --> 02:16.740
Those were all lies told to lure you all here.

02:17.720 --> 02:19.240
No...

02:19.910 --> 02:24.530
Or maybe it's the fantasy of a girl 
who still believes she's alive.

02:28.290 --> 02:29.420
They'll pay for this.

02:30.000 --> 02:31.890
I will use this power

02:31.890 --> 02:36.320
to change this absurd Tower.

02:45.110 --> 02:47.260
Cassano...

04:18.980 --> 04:22.990
<b>Episode 25</b>

04:18.980 --> 04:22.990
<b>Return of the King</b>

04:31.990 --> 04:34.440
A way to kill that smoky bastard?!

04:34.440 --> 04:35.800
Keep your voice down.

04:35.800 --> 04:37.540
We don't want him to know what we're up to.

04:37.540 --> 04:40.170
Just hurry up and tell me how to do it!

04:41.050 --> 04:43.750
Did you buy that spear at the shop?

04:43.750 --> 04:46.050
Yeah. More importantly—

04:46.280 --> 04:47.050
What's its name?

04:48.530 --> 04:51.600
I think it was... Mad Shocker?

04:53.500 --> 04:55.560
You idiot! That's a projectile!

04:55.810 --> 04:59.060
Pro...jectile? What?!

05:00.760 --> 05:02.940
No, maybe that's good for now.

05:02.940 --> 05:04.210
"Good"?

05:04.210 --> 05:08.420
Listen closely. When I give the signal, 
throw that thing along my Lighthouse.

05:08.420 --> 05:09.200
You got that?

05:09.660 --> 05:11.450
Let's finish this quickly...

05:12.050 --> 05:14.550
so the three of us can go home.

05:24.190 --> 05:27.000
Finally, our millennia-old desire...

05:27.450 --> 05:28.580
Now, gator!

05:28.580 --> 05:30.640
I'm not an alligator!

05:30.920 --> 05:32.740
Take this!

05:35.330 --> 05:36.890
<i>It teleported?</i>

05:41.160 --> 05:42.400
Have you forgotten?

05:42.400 --> 05:44.150
You bastard!

05:49.350 --> 05:51.410
Have you forsaken the hostage?

05:52.350 --> 05:54.660
Normally I would, but...

05:55.800 --> 05:58.380
The White Heavenly Mirror?!

06:02.310 --> 06:08.680
Anyone whose heart is pierced 
by this blade is sealed inside it.

06:08.680 --> 06:12.180
You should be more careful 
with your hostages.

06:13.730 --> 06:17.150
I never needed a hostage to fight you anyway!

06:17.150 --> 06:18.730
I'll kill you!

06:22.220 --> 06:23.400
<i>Are you ready yet, Bam?</i>

06:27.080 --> 06:28.360
Die!

06:28.360 --> 06:29.860
Blue turtle!

06:35.810 --> 06:36.990
Finally.

06:42.290 --> 06:43.090
<i>Bam?</i>

06:50.660 --> 06:52.390
What a mess.

06:52.390 --> 06:53.850
Should I tell Viole?

06:54.500 --> 06:56.770
No, FUG is paying me.

06:56.770 --> 06:59.390
But I need Viole...

06:59.390 --> 07:00.890
Horyang!

07:01.220 --> 07:03.130
Horyang!

07:04.030 --> 07:05.060
He's not here, either.

07:15.100 --> 07:17.360
Endorsi, change of plans.

07:18.040 --> 07:20.410
Buying time doesn't suit us.

07:21.400 --> 07:25.170
So let's take them down quickly 
and walk away from this place.

07:27.670 --> 07:30.770
It's my new sword. Don't underestimate it.

07:31.680 --> 07:34.930
That's fine with me,
but where did this come from?

07:35.500 --> 07:41.150
You've heard why FUG trained 
Bam into Viole, haven't you?

07:48.310 --> 07:51.950
In other words, you feel like 
teaching them a lesson?

07:54.730 --> 07:59.450
Now that you mention it,
you blonde traitorous scumbag...

07:59.450 --> 08:02.210
Don't you dare smile in my presence!

08:04.230 --> 08:06.840
Gosh, you're such dummies.

08:06.840 --> 08:09.960
You two don't stand a chance 
against the Mad Dog.

08:18.030 --> 08:21.350
Idiots! That'll never work.

08:21.680 --> 08:25.350
No, it worked against the dogs around him.

08:27.360 --> 08:30.110
You're even dumber than I thought.

08:30.110 --> 08:33.610
Quit yapping and follow me, you mongrel!

08:38.870 --> 08:39.790
Don't tell me...

08:39.790 --> 08:44.900
You may be unbeatable, but if you're 
attacked and fall from this height...

08:44.900 --> 08:45.540
Right?

08:46.420 --> 08:49.040
Now, it's time to end this...

08:52.170 --> 08:54.880
so I can go on my date!

09:00.560 --> 09:02.180
The Thorn showed itself...

09:02.180 --> 09:04.730
Black turtle, are you all right?

09:04.730 --> 09:05.540
Yes.

09:25.590 --> 09:28.210
I shall grant you my shadow.

09:28.490 --> 09:33.200
As one who had everything taken from him 
by the Ten Families, you deserve it.

09:33.200 --> 09:37.240
Power is granted to those worthy of it.

09:38.500 --> 09:40.720
Allow me to test you.

09:42.720 --> 09:47.480
To see if you're worthy 
of wielding that power!

09:49.480 --> 09:52.080
You cannot evade this ability.

09:53.930 --> 09:55.270
<i>Then I'll have to stop it!</i>

09:55.940 --> 09:57.950
I told you, you can't control me!

10:09.140 --> 10:11.460
I thought he couldn't be controlled.

10:11.460 --> 10:15.820
The unleashed Thorn stopped 
his unstable flow.

10:16.500 --> 10:19.470
He's clearly become stronger.

10:20.630 --> 10:22.990
So you were chosen.

10:23.630 --> 10:25.060
It's time.

10:25.060 --> 10:27.440
You will work with the agents of the Elders

10:27.440 --> 10:30.270
to complete the Thorn 
at the Workshop Battle.

10:31.270 --> 10:33.690
Finally, our greatest wish 
will be fulfilled...

10:34.870 --> 10:39.750
That power should be given 
to one truly worthy of it.

10:39.750 --> 10:43.870
I can tell. You are...

10:45.370 --> 10:48.120
not our god.

10:48.120 --> 10:51.170
No, I am not your god,

10:51.550 --> 10:55.630
because your god is a fantasy 
created by your weakness.

10:56.420 --> 10:57.630
You brat.

10:58.140 --> 10:59.630
Die!

10:59.630 --> 11:00.630
I don't think so!

11:00.630 --> 11:01.550
Gator!

11:01.550 --> 11:02.800
I'm not an alligator!

11:02.800 --> 11:05.660
I am the great Rak Wraithraiser!

11:07.140 --> 11:10.210
You called me your god, 
and then you rejected me!

11:10.210 --> 11:13.520
I've had enough of pretending to be a god!

11:32.500 --> 11:35.750
They weren't kidding about 
you having a body of steel.

11:37.000 --> 11:39.140
Endorsi Jahad...

11:39.140 --> 11:44.010
So Reflejo ended in failure. 
How disappointing.

11:44.250 --> 11:47.860
We shall fulfill your greatest wish.

11:52.270 --> 11:54.090
Are you all right, black turtle?

11:55.010 --> 11:55.860
Yes.

11:56.200 --> 11:58.340
The burden on your body 
must still be significant.

12:01.320 --> 12:06.480
Gods sometimes construct fates 
that I cannot laugh about.

12:07.450 --> 12:10.290
Power has been granted 
to one who is unworthy.

12:11.180 --> 12:12.860
His eyes...

12:13.290 --> 12:17.750
If God has made a mistake, 
then I must simply correct it.

12:18.300 --> 12:22.320
My eyes! My eyes!

12:22.320 --> 12:28.300
<i>My heart wavered for just a moment 
when I saw that brilliant beauty.</i>

12:29.330 --> 12:32.980
<i>As punishment for looking upon a princess 
of the Ten Families with my unworthy eyes,</i>

12:32.980 --> 12:36.060
<i>I lost both eyes and my family.</i>

12:37.930 --> 12:45.220
<i>I could never accept how someone 
so cruel possessed such beauty.</i>

12:48.590 --> 12:52.970
Power is granted to those worthy of it.

12:54.670 --> 12:57.750
A solution will be poured 
over this area shortly.

12:58.890 --> 13:00.750
They're going to melt the Thorn?

13:02.090 --> 13:07.490
You will die with me,
along with our greatest wish!

13:10.900 --> 13:12.050
Stop what you're doing.

13:13.190 --> 13:16.060
Abandon the match or else.

13:16.060 --> 13:19.520
How brazen of you, swordsman.

13:19.520 --> 13:23.280
I'm just brazenly doing 
the same thing you did.

13:23.500 --> 13:25.290
Can't you tell?

13:26.530 --> 13:31.410
We've won, Mr. Strongest E-Rank Ranker.

13:33.050 --> 13:36.820
Fine. We lost this time.

13:36.820 --> 13:39.920
Anyway, why don't you go run to your friends?

13:40.320 --> 13:43.170
The man you're supposed to go on 
your date with is about to die.

13:44.140 --> 13:45.390
What is that?

13:46.170 --> 13:48.180
Hurry! We're getting out of here!

13:50.370 --> 13:52.430
Hey! We can't get out!

13:52.430 --> 13:54.180
Did you plan this from the start?

13:55.850 --> 13:58.190
Shibisu, have you found the hostages?

13:58.190 --> 13:59.550
Not yet. What about you?

13:59.550 --> 14:00.830
<i>We have a problem.</i>

14:00.830 --> 14:02.750
<i>The solution will be poured soon.</i>

14:02.750 --> 14:05.190
<i>If we don't get out of here 
right now, we'll all die!</i>

14:05.190 --> 14:07.320
What? What are you talking about?

14:07.320 --> 14:08.970
<i>I'll explain the details later.</i>

14:08.970 --> 14:11.200
<i>Where's Endorsi? We need her Bongbong.</i>

14:11.200 --> 14:13.430
<i>I still can't get in touch with her.</i>

14:14.220 --> 14:16.380
<i>In any case, find the hostages 
as quickly as you can.</i>

14:16.380 --> 14:17.460
<i>I'm counting on you!</i>

14:17.460 --> 14:19.580
What should we do? 
We need to find them soon.

14:19.580 --> 14:21.480
Hey, where do you think you're looking?

14:21.980 --> 14:24.000
The hostages are this way!

14:24.000 --> 14:25.710
Aren't you FUG?

14:25.710 --> 14:27.970
Follow me! Hurry!

14:27.970 --> 14:30.670
You're our enemy. We can't trust you.

14:30.670 --> 14:31.970
Oh, come on!

14:32.210 --> 14:36.350
I'm throwing away 100 
million points to help you!

14:36.350 --> 14:39.120
Now hurry up before I change my mind!

14:42.430 --> 14:44.770
<i>Khun, we've found the hostages!</i>

14:44.770 --> 14:46.580
Nice work!

14:46.580 --> 14:47.490
What about Endorsi?

14:47.490 --> 14:49.400
<i>I'm on my way to you.</i>

14:49.720 --> 14:50.990
Endorsi...

14:50.990 --> 14:53.380
But my Bongbong isn't working.

14:53.380 --> 14:54.430
<i>What?!</i>

14:54.430 --> 14:56.490
I might've been too rough with it.

14:56.490 --> 14:58.090
<i>What are we supposed to do, then?</i>

14:58.090 --> 15:00.330
I don't know, but wait for me!

15:00.330 --> 15:02.020
You'd better not die on me!

15:02.290 --> 15:05.330
<i>There's no way I'm letting you go this time!</i>

15:08.980 --> 15:11.310
Hey, how long are we going to wait?

15:11.310 --> 15:13.390
It's been more than five minutes.

15:13.390 --> 15:14.760
Let's hurry up and go.

15:14.760 --> 15:17.040
Just be quiet and wait.

15:17.790 --> 15:19.270
Hey, isn't that...

15:24.030 --> 15:25.020
Could it be...

15:25.680 --> 15:27.170
A FUG Ranker?

15:27.780 --> 15:31.530
Quant! Contact Hatzling! 
We have a situation D!

15:31.840 --> 15:34.960
Quickly! If we don't hurry,
it'll be too late!

15:53.800 --> 15:55.980
What the hell is going on?

15:55.980 --> 15:58.220
You're dumping the solution on Rankers?

15:58.220 --> 16:00.060
Regardless of the reason, 
that's crossing the line!

16:00.060 --> 16:03.030
Stop it right away. 
Otherwise, our contract—

16:03.030 --> 16:05.060
I'm glad to hear that.

16:05.060 --> 16:10.140
I was just thinking about 
dissolving the contract.

16:10.140 --> 16:15.450
After all, I already gave the 
compression flask to someone else.

16:15.450 --> 16:16.570
You did what?!

16:16.570 --> 16:22.720
A good deal was offered to me 
while the match was on hold.

16:22.720 --> 16:24.960
You can't be serious! Where did they go?

16:24.960 --> 16:28.210
Who knows? Perhaps he already left.

16:28.210 --> 16:31.460
You tricked us!

16:31.680 --> 16:36.900
Hardly. I simply made a deal with 
someone who offered me good terms.

16:36.900 --> 16:38.470
I'm running a business, after all.

16:39.250 --> 16:40.500
You'd better prepare yourself.

16:40.500 --> 16:43.480
You know what happens when you 
cross a Workshop Battle host?

16:43.480 --> 16:48.480
Is there anyone important 
here to protect you?

16:49.610 --> 16:54.770
Perhaps I should destroy the entire 
ship as well, once I acquire the Thorn.

17:08.390 --> 17:11.280
<i>You bastard!</i>

17:22.310 --> 17:24.230
Did it stop?

17:24.230 --> 17:25.710
What happened?

17:25.710 --> 17:27.900
Good. You're all right.

17:28.420 --> 17:30.650
Ro, why...

17:30.900 --> 17:33.150
I'm here to save my students.

17:34.400 --> 17:37.160
I will buy you time.

17:37.430 --> 17:39.990
Quant's floating ship is on its way to you.

17:39.990 --> 17:43.160
Take the hostages and go.

17:43.600 --> 17:46.520
Hurry. I'm dealing with a Ranker.

17:46.520 --> 17:48.220
There's only so much I can do.

17:51.040 --> 17:53.300
Shibisu, where are the hostages?

17:53.300 --> 17:54.670
We got them all.

17:54.670 --> 17:57.180
<i>Good. There's a floating ship coming.</i>

17:57.180 --> 17:58.800
<i>You and Vespa make your way to it.</i>

17:58.800 --> 18:00.790
<i>Got it. What about you guys?</i>

18:00.790 --> 18:02.260
We'll wait for Endorsi.

18:02.260 --> 18:05.810
For now, our only way out 
of here is her Bongbong.

18:05.810 --> 18:06.850
<i>But what if—</i>

18:06.850 --> 18:07.920
Don't worry.

18:07.920 --> 18:12.350
Even if it doesn't work, we'll find a way 
for all of us to get out of here, so go.

18:14.510 --> 18:16.680
What am I supposed to do about this?

18:20.470 --> 18:22.050
Why won't it work?

18:22.050 --> 18:24.670
Think. There must be a reason.

18:24.670 --> 18:26.710
Is it out of power?

18:26.710 --> 18:29.370
But there's no energy source to charge it.

18:47.300 --> 18:49.560
Why do you get in our way?

18:51.060 --> 18:53.970
If it's for some paltry 
sense of righteousness,

18:53.970 --> 18:56.070
then you're being foolishly reckless.

18:56.070 --> 18:59.400
Reckless? You seem confused.

19:00.350 --> 19:05.080
Our allies are currently hacking the 
security cameras aboard the <i>Archimedes</i>

19:05.080 --> 19:10.580
and broadcasting everything happening 
here to all monitors in the Tower.

19:10.870 --> 19:15.840
Every Ranker and powerful person is 
watching the atrocities you're committing.

19:15.840 --> 19:19.840
Though, naturally, I've concealed 
the details about the Thorn.

19:19.840 --> 19:21.840
Bastard...

19:21.840 --> 19:26.170
This wouldn't have happened if 
you hadn't crossed the line.

19:26.170 --> 19:28.140
Who's reckless now?

19:31.850 --> 19:34.880
Help seems to have arrived, 
but it's pointless.

19:34.880 --> 19:37.830
This place will collapse soon.

19:37.830 --> 19:39.700
Are you satisfied?

19:40.610 --> 19:44.620
Does it satisfy you to be used and then die?

19:44.620 --> 19:45.990
Of course.

19:47.490 --> 19:52.370
Being used is one way 
to live a life of hope.

19:52.370 --> 19:54.400
You're wrong. That's not—

19:54.400 --> 19:56.400
You know nothing!

19:56.400 --> 20:01.430
After acquiring such power, 
you still do nothing!

20:01.430 --> 20:03.890
You know nothing about me!

20:04.230 --> 20:06.410
I hate God!

20:06.410 --> 20:16.310
Give me that power, and I would gladly 
give my life to change the Tower!

20:21.150 --> 20:22.650
Damn it!

20:27.140 --> 20:28.120
Bam!

20:31.340 --> 20:35.010
For our greatest wish...

20:37.010 --> 20:38.470
Viole...

20:50.390 --> 20:51.390
Viole.

20:51.890 --> 20:53.400
Help me.

20:53.400 --> 20:55.900
Hey, you're pretty good.

20:56.220 --> 20:57.770
In fact, why don't we work together?

20:58.270 --> 21:00.940
We overcome all challenges together.

21:01.170 --> 21:03.080
That's what teammates do.

21:03.780 --> 21:06.320
I have to climb the Tower!

21:06.320 --> 21:09.330
I'm gonna reach the top of the Tower!

21:09.750 --> 21:11.540
I'll become the king of this Tower

21:12.170 --> 21:15.820
and change the unjustness 
that made things this way!

21:16.630 --> 21:21.670
I want to make this a place 
where we can laugh together.

21:21.670 --> 21:26.140
I want to see a bigger sky, too.

21:24.360 --> 21:29.640
Viole! Viole! Viole!

21:30.050 --> 21:31.700
Jue Viole Grace.

21:32.840 --> 21:34.840
I will crush FUG.

21:40.690 --> 21:43.150
Let's go, Viole.

21:44.740 --> 21:46.710
Bam!

21:49.880 --> 21:54.700
<i>This is fine. Now I can finally...</i>

21:55.210 --> 21:57.810
Let's go home, Mister Useless.

22:03.730 --> 22:04.410
Okay.

23:37.850 --> 23:39.490
Now we can go on our date.

23:38.990 --> 23:41.250
<b>Next Time
The Dawn of Departure</b>
